New Investigations Planned by Strategist:

  1. Vulnerability analysis of Timelock
     Priority: 10 | Impact: high | Category: aspect
     Reasoning: WHY NOW: Timelock is a critical permission boundary controlling 
execution of governance actions, and its queued-hash, timing, and self-call 
semantics can determine whether unauthorized or prematurely queued actions are 
executable. EXIT CRITERIA: Trace every externally reachable queue, cancel, and 
execute path; verify hash uniqueness, timestamp bounds, admin/guardian 
authorization, state cleanup before calls, and delay-update restrictions; 
document any exploitable bypass or conclude these invariants hold.

